            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"appId\": \"{{appId}}\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"{{timestamp}}\",\n  \"nonce\": \"{{nonce}}\",\n  \"sign\": \"{{sign}}\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"userId\": \"{{userId}}\",\n    \"desiredAmount\": {{desiredAmount}}\n  }\n}"
            },
            "description": "The cheap shape: identify with /openApi/users first, then send the userId alone. It does not work.\n\n2026-09-17, userId 1550194515653763072, after users returned hasMyinfo: true — this returned {\"code\":\"500\",\"msg\":\"System error\"}. The same user succeeded minutes earlier and later when the full myinfo object was sent instead.\n\nQuestion for Ascend: is userId-only supported at all? If so, what makes this 500?"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1c. apply/credit — full myinfo (WORKS)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
